shed in pakistan  the first funerals were held today for  some of the victims two passengers  survived  at least 97 people were killed the pilot  told air traffic control he was having  engine trouble  just before issuing a mayday call one  survivor says the flight proceeded  normally until its descent  when there was a sudden jolt a  profanity-laced video of brazil's  president  is causing new controversy tonight  expresses frustration at his inability  to get information from police  he also vows to change cabinet ministers  if needed to protect his family  the supreme court ordered their footage  be released as part of an investigation  into allegations  the president was trying to interfere in  the federal police  for personal gain bolsonaro isn't taking  the covid19 crisis  seriously calling it a little flu but  the world health organization  disagrees and says south america is a  new epicenter  of the pandemic a number of countries in  that part of the world have seen a major  increase in cases  the change is in large part because  brazil overtook the united kingdom this  week  for third place in overall number of  coven 19  cases we've seen many south american  countries with  increasing numbers of cases and  and clearly there's a concern across  many of those countries but certainly  the most affected  is brazil at this point brazil now has  the fastest growth of infections  in the world there are more than 330  000 confirmed cases in the country and  more than 21 000 people have died from  the virus  but experts believe those numbers are  likely higher  because of a lack of testing still ahead  the campaign to focus on health  not hate  prime minister justin trudeau is calling  on canadians to stand up  and speak out against racism across the  country attacks targeting  asian communities have been on the rise  ever since the pandemic began  in vancouver alone 29 anti-asian hate  crimes have been reported  so far this year in 2019 only  four were reported in